WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:05.220
The new season of Yellowstone has lots&nbsp;
of fans talking — and they don't have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:10.680
good things to say! Here's why fans of the show&nbsp;
are fed up with this ongoing sibling rivalry.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:16.020
Yellowstone fans have had some bleak opinions&nbsp;
about Season 5 of the show since it began airing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:20.340
in November of 2022. Many loyal viewers&nbsp;
have begun to call the program out for its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:24.780
repetitive storytelling tropes, which mainly&nbsp;
feature the Dutton clan suffering mightily,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:29.640
then claiming rip-roaring revenge on their&nbsp;
enemies. Fans are annoyed, for instance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:33.600
with the fact that Kayce Dutton and his wife,&nbsp;
Monica are currently suffering through the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:38.640
aftermath of a miscarriage, which feels like&nbsp;
an unnecessary trauma that doesn't do anything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:43.680
to drive either character's stories forward&nbsp;
and just piles more misery onto their heads.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:48.420
The storyline is one of a number of stories&nbsp;
that are feeling tiresome to some members of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:53.160
the audience, according to many posts on social&nbsp;
media. At least one relationship on the show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:57.240
in particular, has begun to draw grumbles&nbsp;
from fans, who are getting awfully&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:01.500
exhausted from the endless conflict&nbsp;
between these two Dutton siblings.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:06.060
Beth Dutton understandably holds a grudge&nbsp;
against her half-brother, Jamie. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:10.440
he's the reason why she can't have biological&nbsp;
children after he took her to a clinic on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:15.720
Broken Rock reservation after a teenage tryst with&nbsp;
Rip resulted in her pregnancy. She was sterilized&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:21.360
after an abortion was performed at Jamie's&nbsp;
request, and without her expressed consent.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:27.420
Add on a heaping helping of sibling rivalry and&nbsp;
misplaced loyalties and you have a woman bent on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:32.520
revenge. When Jamie shows up to bail Beth out of&nbsp;
jail during the fourth episode of season five, she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:38.820
realizes he's been caring for the child he shares&nbsp;
with his ex-campaign manager. Thus, Beth vows to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:43.800
take the kid from Jamie just to rob him of the&nbsp;
pleasure of parenthood that she has been denied.

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:49.200
But fans of Yellowstone are getting sick of Beth's&nbsp;
vendetta, no matter how understandable it is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:54.180
as Jamie has shown remorse for his horrible&nbsp;
deed. On Twitter, many fans are both exhausted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:58.080
by the storyline and the character's&nbsp;
treatment of each other. One user wrote:

00:02:08.719 --> 00:02:13.431
"Next time you see him you can kiss him&nbsp;
goodbye because he's as good as gone."

00:02:13.431 --> 00:02:17.280
Another Twitter user even called it the&nbsp;
most irritating part of the program.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:21.300
Some fans who are sick of the sibling&nbsp;
rivalry storyline think it would help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:25.500
if Jamie worked up some courage around his&nbsp;
sister. One Yellowstone watcher tweeted:

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:40.920
On the Yellowstone subreddit, the opinions from&nbsp;
fans weren't much better. One redditor wrote:

00:02:47.601 --> 00:02:49.860
Another redditor had an idea for how to turn the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:54.060
Beth-Jamie situation into something new&nbsp;
by bringing in a third party, writing,

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:02.100
This would undoubtedly change&nbsp;
the dynamic of the storyline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:08.220
but it could have drastic repercussions for all&nbsp;
three characters, especially Jamie. Some viewers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:12.000
took a different route and offered up other&nbsp;
storylines that the series should introduce&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:16.500
to get away from all this repetitive Beth-Jamie&nbsp;
nonsense. One person suggested on reddit:

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.340
They'll have to keep watching&nbsp;
to see how it all pans out.&nbsp;&nbsp;

